---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Eyebrow from './Eyebrow.astro';
import HarnessPipeline from './HarnessPipeline.astro';

const checks = [
  {
    n: '01',
    title: 'Closed',
    body:
      'Re-scan after the patch. Is the original finding actually gone, or did it move somewhere else in the file?',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    title: 'Behaviour held',
    body:
      'We generate test cases the agent never saw and run the patched code against those.',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    title: 'No regression',
    body:
      'Re-scan the change itself. Fixes routinely trade one finding for another.',
  },
  {
    n: '04',
    title: 'Provenance clean',
    body:
      'Which agent authored the change, under what token scope, and does the diff show injection markers: self-config edits, unexpected file touches, credential access.',
  },
];
---

<Section id="how-it-works" tint>
  <Eyebrow class="reveal">How it works</Eyebrow>

  <h2 class="h2 reveal" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">Findings in. Verdict out.</h2>

  <p class="lede reveal mt-6" style="--reveal-delay:120ms">
    Four checks that nobody runs today, on every AI-authored change.
  </p>

  {/* A punch card. Four checks, struck in order, mono and ruled rather than
      four cards in a row. The struck marks are this section's one accent. */}
  <ol class="card mt-14">
    {
      checks.map((check, i) => (
        <li class="card-row reveal" style={`--reveal-delay:${i * 60}ms`}>
          <span class="card-n">{check.n}</span>

          <span class="punch punch-struck" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="4 12 10 18 20 6"></polyline></svg>
          </span>

          <div class="card-body">
            <h3 class="card-title">{check.title}</h3>
            <p class="card-text">{check.body}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <p
    class="mono reveal mt-8 border-l-2 border-line pl-5 text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-fg-2"
    style="--reveal-delay:240ms;max-width:62ch"
  >
    If you let a student write their own exam, they will pass it. You test them on
    questions they have not seen.
  </p>

  <div class="reveal mt-16 border-t border-line pt-7 lg:mt-20">
    <p class="micro mb-3">Inside the harness</p>

    <p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.62]" style="max-width:62ch">
      Where the cases the agent never saw actually come from.
    </p>

    <HarnessPipeline />
  </div>

  <div class="reveal mt-16 border-t border-line pt-7 lg:mt-20" style="max-width:76ch">
    <p class="micro mb-3">The second failure mode, and why check 04 exists</p>

    <h3 class="font-display text-[21px] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.015em] lg:text-[24px]">
      The fixer is itself an attack surface.
    </h3>

    <div class="prose-body mt-4 space-y-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.65] text-fg-2">
      <p>
        A flaw in the Claude Code GitHub Action let a single opened GitHub issue hand an
        attacker write access to any repository running it. CVSS v4.0 7.8, fixed in
        claude-code-action v1.0.94.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing about a patch like that looks wrong to a scanner, because the scanner is
        not the thing being attacked. When the agent writing your fix can be instructed by
        the code it is reading,{' '}
        <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">provenance stops being paperwork</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .card {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .card-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 20px minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 16px;
      align-items: start;
      padding: 20px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .card-n {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: var(--t-meta);
      letter-spacing: var(--t-meta-track);
      color: var(--fg-3);
      padding-top: 4px;
    }

    .card-title {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      line-height: 1.4;
    }

    .card-text {
      margin-top: 6px;
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--fg-2);
      max-width: 68ch;
    }

    @media (min-width: 720px) {
      .card-row {
        grid-template-columns: auto 20px minmax(0, 15ch) minmax(0, 1fr);
        align-items: baseline;
        gap: 20px;
      }
      .card-body {
        display: contents;
      }
      .card-text {
        margin-top: 0;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Section>
